26b8f3a9 Workgroup size: with LocalSizeId the size comes from its constants, also when a WorkgroupSize builtin composite exists (the literal sizes are 0 then, and the threadgroup was 1 thread), and a dimension is specialized only when its constant is a specialization constant (a composite of plain constants read as specialization constant 0)
6cbe8687 Geometry pipelines: ignore pMultisampleState when rasterization is disabled, as the other pipeline paths do. Vulkan allows it to be null then, and newMTLGeometryRenderPipelineDescriptor read its rasterizationSamples: DXVK 3.1's D3D11 stream output with no rasterized stream (a passthrough geometry shader with rasterizer discard) crashed in vkCreateGraphicsPipelines
84a59b28 Geometry shader limits: Vulkan's minimums (32 invocations, 64 input and 128 output components, 256 output vertices, 1024 total output components) instead of 0. Geometry shaders run as Metal mesh pipelines, one mesh threadgroup per invocation and one mesh of at most 256 vertices as its output, but every maxGeometry* limit read 0, so any geometry shader pipeline exceeded what the device reported
f799fa19 Residency set: adds are counted per allocation and the last removal removes it, whatever heap it is placed in at that point; removals decided by the current heap left a resource added before its heap became resident in the set after it was freed, or removed one that was never added, and the next commit faulted in the driver (Dragon's Dogma 2's first vkQueueSubmit2: AGXG16GFamilyResidencySet _commitAddedAllocations)
6bd2d616 Metal Shader Converter bridge: a converted draw unmarks descriptor sets 0 to 2 of the vertex and fragment stages, whose buffer indexes its heaps and top-level argument buffer overwrite, so the next SPIR-V draw in the render pass binds its sets again instead of reading them from the heaps (GPU page faults in God of War Ragnarök's particle passes); compute already rebinds sets on every pipeline change
9d93a852 METALSHARP_TRACE=gpu: a debug signpost before each draw and dispatch names its shaders (Metal Shader Converter pipelines by VKD3D-Proton's DXIL hashes), and a faulted encoder's last eight signposts are logged as warnings
7e7fa37e Descriptor sets: the size (aux) buffer fits in the set. Emulated sampler reduction keeps a mode per sampler there, but sets whose size buffer only samplers use never counted it (no aux offsets to recompute the size from), and variable-count sets put it after n descriptor-plus-aux elements instead of n descriptors, so writing the last samplers of a variable sampler array (VKD3D-Proton's sampler heap: element 1021 of 1024) wrote past the set into the next allocation. The pool keeps each set's first aux entry, and a set whose only size-buffer user is a sampler gets its pointer to the size buffer
472fe038 Metal Shader Converter bridge for graphics: a pipeline of a converted vertex shader and, optionally, a converted fragment shader (blob stages 1 and 2) is built from the converter's libraries; the vertex blob's table of semantics and Vulkan locations, with the converter's reflection, moves each Vulkan vertex attribute to its stage-in attribute; draws bind the push constants (the top-level argument buffer) at index 2 and the heaps at 0 and 1 of both stages, and flip the viewport's Y instead of the shader, as SPIR-V vertex shaders do; generated-command draws with such a pipeline are skipped
717823d7 Metal Shader Converter bridge, contract version 2: the blob header gains the push constants offset of two heap addresses, and a pipeline whose blob has one binds the CBV/SRV/UAV and sampler heaps it points at as Metal buffers 0 and 1 (kIRDescriptorHeapBindPoint, kIRSamplerHeapBindPoint), so SM 6.6 shaders that index ResourceDescriptorHeap and SamplerDescriptorHeap directly run converted; version 1 blobs still work
57eab612 Metal Shader Converter bridge (docs/MSC-BRIDGE-CONTRACT.md in MetalSharp-Wine): a shader module whose code is a DXIL blob (magic 0x4D534358, DXIL plus a flattened root signature) makes a compute pipeline from Apple's converter (libmetalirconverter.dylib, loaded at runtime): newLibraryWithData skips the MSL front-end compile, which took 0.4-1.7 s per large shader; such a pipeline binds only its push constants, the converter's top-level argument buffer, at index 2; VK_NVX_image_view_handle returns Metal resource IDs for image views, samplers and texel buffer views; the converter's Apache-2.0 headers are included
51519bc0 Large temporary buffers given back are kept for reuse up to 512 MB per process (freeing each one made God of War allocate about 74 buffers of 16-32 MB a second); binary archives leave out mesh pipelines too (Metal can't serialize them: 'missing vertex stage'), and adds wait until the app has compiled nothing for 2 s, so they don't slow the compiles a game waits on
35b86fcb Fixes from five traced games: passes without attachments keep pixels times layers to 2^30 (The Witcher 3 failed every frame needing 17 GiB); draws with a tessellation + geometry pipeline are skipped (built as geometry, drawn as tessellation: Ghostrunner's queue stopped); indexed indirect tessellation sizes its buffers from the bound index buffer, and temporary buffers of 16 MB or more are released after use (RDR2 grew by gigabytes); binary archives leave out pipelines without a fragment stage (they broke every save), save every minute with at most 256 adds waiting, and save at exit; timestamp pools use several 4096-sample counter buffers; METALSHARP_TRACE=gpu names a failed command buffer's encoders, memory logs large temporary buffers
5091a516 VK_EXT_device_generated_commands: indirect command buffers come from a device pool (power-of-two capacities, up to 512 MB kept free) instead of a new one per vkCmdExecuteGeneratedCommandsEXT(): each is about 1.25 KB per command (82 MB at 65,536), and RDR2's GPU memory grew by gigabytes once frames slowed; METALSHARP_TRACE=memory logs each new one
8d0fe8eb Reapply "MetalSharp trace flag: warnings and errors always reach moltenvk.log while tracing (an app's MVK_CONFIG_LOG_LEVEL hid RDR2's GPU timeouts); the GPU watchdog names a failed command buffer's error; memory samples this process's footprint and the system's swap and paging every 5 s"
9eac6d20 Revert "MetalSharp trace flag: warnings and errors always reach moltenvk.log while tracing (an app's MVK_CONFIG_LOG_LEVEL hid RDR2's GPU timeouts); the GPU watchdog names a failed command buffer's error; memory samples this process's footprint and the system's swap and paging every 5 s"
57f16a0b MetalSharp trace flag: warnings and errors always reach moltenvk.log while tracing (an app's MVK_CONFIG_LOG_LEVEL hid RDR2's GPU timeouts); the GPU watchdog names a failed command buffer's error; memory samples this process's footprint and the system's swap and paging every 5 s
eee37003 MetalSharp trace flag: present times are signed differences; presented handlers can run out of order, which wrapped the unsigned ones
dce18df9 MetalSharp trace flag: METALSHARP_TRACE=<category>[+heavy] writes moltenvk.log next to VKD3D-Proton's vkd3d.log (one folder per game) and turns on what each category needs: per-present drawable wait and on-screen timing, memory and heap allocation, buffer and image creation, host waits on fences and timeline semaphores, per-pipeline Metal compile times, a GPU hang watchdog that reports command buffers stuck waiting to be scheduled or running, the Vulkan call trace, render pass and texture debug output
1e5ffbe1 Geometry pipelines: no implicit point size on the object stage, whose payload then had a member the mesh stage's lacked; Metal's compiler crashed on point-list geometry pipelines (Elden Ring)
d1cb9e95 Tessellation with point or isoline output takes a winding order by default: points and lines have none, and D3D hull shaders emitting them don't declare one (The Witcher 3's pipeline failed to reflect)
84971d78 Geometry pipelines: the object stage's vertex fetch follows each attribute's storage format (an R8G8B8A8_UNORM attribute is four bytes; packed R10G10B10A2 had no entry and failed with 0 components) and its input rate
a15bc548 Translated vertex bindings are reserved only for static strides: a dynamic stride counted every offset attribute and pushed the implicit buffers onto descriptor buffers
854fe1fd Buffer state per draw and render pass restarts: an identical vkCmdBindDescriptorSets changes nothing and a changed one invalidates only the sets and implicit buffers (BufferSize, DynamicOffset, Swizzle) of the stages that changed; unchanged push constants are skipped and changed ones invalidate only the stages in stageFlags; zero-divisor vertex buffers and emulated depth bounds bind through the checked binders (the zero-divisor path left the binding cache stale); host-read memory barriers return at once on unified memory; temporary buffers (including vkCmdUpdateBuffer's) return to their pool from one completion handler per command buffer without setPurgeableState toggles, and fills of four equal bytes use a blit fill; heaps are made resident and resources placed in them skip per-resource residency adds and removes, the rest commit once before each Metal command buffer, and removing a buffer from its memory is O(1); imported host memory is untracked when a residency set is in use; and the indirect-count conversions of a render pass's draws run in one compute encoder before the Metal pass starts instead of ending and restarting it per draw (MVK_CONFIG_HOIST_DRAW_CONVERSIONS=0 turns it off). Targeted Vulkan CTS subsets (copies and fills, push constants, indirect draws, mesh draws, memory, dynamic descriptors) match the unmodified build.
ef956862 The binary archive has a queue of its own: its adds (a compile each) ran on the implicit pipeline cache's queue, and a game's thousands of them kept the cache from being written for as long as it compiled (God of War Ragnarok: nothing in 3 minutes); adds still waiting when the device goes are dropped instead of holding up its destruction
a0fa30f5 Pipeline caches keep their work across launches and rebuilds: the implicit cache is also written once a minute while pipelines keep arriving (a game closed, crashed or killed during a long precompile saved nothing, and the next launch compiled every shader again; MVK_CONFIG_PIPELINE_CACHE_SAVE_INTERVAL), it and the pipeline cache UUID are keyed on a hash of the sources that decide what a cache holds when the build gives one (MVK_PIPELINE_CACHE_SOURCES_HASH, scripts/moltenvk-cache-key.sh) instead of the build UUID that every rebuild changed, each library keeps its compiled metallib next to its MSL (Metal's private libraryDataContents), loaded instead of running Metal's front end (God of War Ragnarok's kernels: 187 ms from MSL, 0.03 ms from the metallib; MVK_CONFIG_CACHE_COMPILED_SHADERS=0 keeps only the MSL), and compiled pipelines go into a device-wide MTLBinaryArchive next to the cache, looked up first with MTLPipelineOptionFailOnBinaryArchiveMiss so a relaunch skips Metal's back end (MVK_CONFIG_BINARY_ARCHIVE=0 disables it)
37499e09 The Cereal size check expects the padding CompilerMSL::Options and the structs holding it have now (3 bytes more), so it no longer reports them incomplete at every start
900cb052 MVK_CONFIG_DGC_STATS=1 logs, every 2000 vkCmdExecuteGeneratedCommandsEXT() calls, how many sequences they allowed and whether a count buffer limited them: what an application's GPU-driven work looks like
0824f472 The application's dispatches run concurrently, as Vulkan lets them: a pipeline barrier between dispatches is already a memory barrier in the compute encoder and any other ends it, and in a serial encoder each dispatch waited for the previous one, leaving the GPU idle between small dispatches (d3d12_perf_probe, 20 compute ExecuteIndirects a frame: GPU 38.4 -> 5.8 ms at 1024 allowed, 64 counted; 4.5 -> 2.1 ms at 64). MVK_CONFIG_CONCURRENT_DISPATCH=0 makes them serial
67a03435 Fragment outputs are converted to their color attachment's kind of number (SPIRV-Cross frag_output_base_types, from the rendering formats): a float output to an integer attachment failed pipeline creation ("output of type float4 is not compatible with a MTLPixelFormatR32Uint color attachment"; VKD3D-Proton's test_render_target_support_validation, an R32_TYPELESS render target)
593fa2cc An image view made through a memory alias (a 2D view of a 3D texture, a block texel view) remembers the image texture it was made from: it is a view of the alias, so its parents never matched the image's texture and the view was released and made again at every use (each render pass's attachments), Metal's texture release waiting on its resource list lock: 38% of God of War Ragnarok's queue encoding time
fbbc4f52 A graphics pipeline's fragment shader library compiles on another thread while its vertex shader converts and compiles: its configuration is made by the same steps (setVertexShaderConfig(), setFragmentShaderConfig(), split out of the add*ShaderToPipeline() functions) and the fragment stage then finds it in the pipeline cache; not for caches the application synchronizes itself. MVK_CONFIG_PARALLEL_STAGE_COMPILE=0 compiles the stages one after the other
f207ae66 Emulated depth bounds tests take their depth snapshot texture from the device, one per queue and kind of depth attachment, which Metal orders between the queue's command buffers: a texture made at every command buffer and every change of depth target took a third of the queue's encoding time in God of War Ragnarok (Metal's resource list lock)
9d3ab08a Shaders are compiled optimized for size (MVK_CONFIG_SHADER_OPTIMIZATION=0 restores Metal's default level): the Metal front end takes about half the time on large shaders (God of War Ragnarok's 1472-line compute shader: 1.07 s, 0.49 s), with the GPU compiler still optimizing behind it; GPU times in the D3D12 probe's shader-heavy scenes are the same
4374d987 The implicit pipeline cache is saved once pipelines stop arriving, in one pass under one hold of the cache's lock: it was rewritten every 3 s while a game compiled (200 MB, a core, and the compile threads waiting on the lock), and a library added between taking the size and writing left the size 0 (VK_INCOMPLETE, "Failed to write 4 bytes to output stream"), also for vkGetPipelineCacheData
8f7f440b Variable-count uniform and storage buffer bindings (BufferAuxSize, sizes kept by binding in the auxiliary buffer) are declared open-ended too: Metal walked VKD3D-Proton's 1,000,000-element SSBO and CBV heap arrays at every pipeline creation, most of its cost in God of War Ragnarok
d8746a56 Texel buffer alignment of a format Metal has no pixel format for (VK_FORMAT_R32G32B32_SFLOAT, D3D12 typed buffers) is the device's limit: Metal asserted and ended the process (God of War Ragnarok on VKD3D-Proton); the view is refused with VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED as before
7189d350 Variable-count argument buffer bindings are declared open-ended in shaders (one element, indexed past, same layout), so Metal doesn't walk 1,000,000-element arrays at every pipeline creation (~200 ms per pipeline with VKD3D-Proton's descriptor heaps)
7afa2158 Push descriptors keep descriptor info copies in the command (no allocation per push) and recording leaves shared pipeline layout reference counts alone when unchanged; optional parallel encoding of a submission's command buffers (MVK_CONFIG_PARALLEL_SUBMIT_ENCODING, off: slower in the D3D12 probe)
939d8d02 Graphics pipelines: reflect shaders through the resolved modules, so stages with an inline VkShaderModuleCreateInfo (maintenance5, as DXVK 2.7 passes them) don't dereference a null module
333fd01f pipelineCacheUUID: last 4 bytes from the binary's build UUID, so caches kept by apps don't outlive a build
20d2a897 Default floating-point functions for NaN-preserving shaders (every DXBC shader from VKD3D-Proton) unless fast math is off
4fb7fb4f Keep dispatch-to-dispatch memory barriers inside the compute encoder; flush timestamps before copying query results
67f3e719 Performance: persistent device-wide pipeline cache, push descriptor implicit buffers, fewer encoder splits
